precept GlobalMeetingScheduler

# A global meeting record for a distributed team. One host schedules the
# meeting from their own timezone; participants in many regions need to see
# the meeting time rendered in their local zone. The canonical time is stored
# as an `instant` (UTC); the host's timezone determines how the local
# rendering is computed via `instant.inZone(timezone)`. The host region's
# business hours are kept as plain `time` values (wall-clock facts in the
# host's region) so the scheduler can flag invitations that fall outside
# acceptable working hours and require the host to acknowledge before the
# meeting can advance.
#
# Constructor pattern: every meeting must arrive with a title, a host, a host
# timezone, a UTC start instant, a duration, and the host region's business
# hours. None of those can be progressively enriched — they are existential
# facts about the meeting.
#
# Demonstrates: `timezone` (IANA identifiers), `zoneddatetime` (host's local
# view of a UTC instant via `instant.inZone(timezone)`), `time` (business
# hours as time-of-day with comparison), `duration` (meeting length and
# instant arithmetic to derive `MeetingEndUtc`), computed fields (`<-`) for
# every derived view of the canonical instant, entry hooks (`to State -> set`)
# for phase timestamps, and a `set of timezone` + `lookup of ~string to timezone`
# pairing for per-participant region awareness.
#
# Case-insensitive identity. Every field that carries an email address is
# declared `~string`. Email addresses are the textbook case-mismatch bug:
# in case-sensitive systems, "Alice@example.com" and "alice@example.com"
# become two separate participants — one shows up in the attendee count
# twice, gets two invitation emails, and the timezone lookup stores two
# entries that drift out of sync. Precept eliminates that bug structurally:
# `set of ~string` collapses both casings to one element, `lookup of ~string`
# resolves both forms to the same key, and the `==`/`!=` operators are
# compile errors on a ~string field — the author cannot accidentally write
# a case-sensitive comparison. The AddParticipant flow below shows the
# pattern: a `contains` guard refuses a duplicate before the row's side
# effects fire, and the CI semantics make that guard work regardless of
# how the email was capitalized.

# ── Meeting identity (existential — set at construction) ──────────────────────
field MeetingId as string notempty maxlength 50
field Title as string notempty maxlength 200
field HostName as string notempty maxlength 200
field HostEmail as ~string notempty maxlength 200

# ── Canonical time ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The single source of truth: the meeting starts at this UTC instant. Every
# participant's local rendering is derived from it via inZone(theirZone).
field MeetingStartUtc as instant
field MeetingDuration as duration

# Host's region — drives the host-facing rendering and the business-hours check.
field HostTimezone as timezone

# Host region's working hours. Captured as time-of-day, not as a UTC instant,
# because business hours are wall-clock facts in the host's region. The
# scheduler flags after-hours meetings via the `IsAfterHoursForHost` signal.
field HostBusinessHoursStart as time
field HostBusinessHoursEnd as time

# ── Derived views of the canonical instant ────────────────────────────────────
# The host sees the meeting time in their own timezone. The proof engine
# keeps these renderings atomically consistent with MeetingStartUtc — change
# the canonical instant and every downstream view updates in lockstep.
field MeetingEndUtc as instant <- MeetingStartUtc + MeetingDuration
field HostLocalStart as zoneddatetime <- MeetingStartUtc.inZone(HostTimezone)
field HostLocalEnd as zoneddatetime <- MeetingEndUtc.inZone(HostTimezone)
field HostLocalDate as date <- HostLocalStart.date
field HostLocalStartTime as time <- HostLocalStart.time
field HostLocalEndTime as time <- HostLocalEnd.time
field HostLocalDayOfWeek as integer <- HostLocalStart.dayOfWeek

# Working-hours signal — true when the meeting's host-local start time falls
# outside the configured working window. Hosts use this to require a confirm.
field IsAfterHoursForHost as boolean <- HostLocalStartTime < HostBusinessHoursStart or HostLocalStartTime >= HostBusinessHoursEnd

# Weekend signal — Saturday (6) or Sunday (7) by ISO weekday. Not gated, but
# surfaced to the UI so the host can think twice about a Sunday meeting.
field IsWeekendForHost as boolean <- HostLocalDayOfWeek >= 6

# ── Participants ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Unique participant timezones — the scheduler renders the meeting time in
# each of these for the invitation email. A `set` collapses duplicates so a
# meeting with five attendees in New York counts as one zone, not five, for
# the rendering loop.
field ParticipantZones as set of timezone

# Membership set — drives the existence check on RemoveParticipant. Pairs
# with ParticipantZoneByEmail as the canonical record per email. Declared
# `set of ~string` so that two events carrying the same email in different
# casings ("Alice@…" and "ALICE@…") resolve to a single set element — the
# proof obligation on AddParticipant's `not contains` guard is discharged
# correctly regardless of the casing the caller used.
field ParticipantEmails as set of ~string

# Per-participant timezone map keyed by email — the source of truth that
# feeds the rendering loop. The scheduler iterates this for the per-recipient
# invite copy. `lookup of ~string to timezone` keys case-insensitively, so
# `put` and `for` always land on the same entry for a given person.
field ParticipantZoneByEmail as lookup of ~string to timezone

field ParticipantCount as integer default 0 nonnegative

# ── After-hours acknowledgement ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# When IsAfterHoursForHost is true at scheduling time, the host must
# acknowledge before Schedule is allowed to complete. This is the closest
# Precept can come to "are you sure?" UI — make it a structural pre-condition.
field AfterHoursAcknowledged as boolean default false

# ── Cancellation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
field CancellationReason as string optional

# ── Audit log ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
field MeetingLog as log of string

# ── Phase timestamps ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
field ScheduledAt as instant optional
field StartedAt as instant optional
field EndedAt as instant optional
field CancelledAt as instant optional

# ── Rules ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
rule HostBusinessHoursEnd > HostBusinessHoursStart because "Business hours end {HostBusinessHoursEnd} must be after business hours start {HostBusinessHoursStart}"
# BUG-008 family: `duration <= '<literal>'` crashes the compiler. Compare via
# the totalHours accessor instead until typed-duration comparisons land.
rule MeetingDuration.totalHours <= 8 because "A scheduled meeting may not exceed 8 hours — longer events should be split or marked as offsites"
# BUG-006: the proof engine doesn't combine the AddParticipant guard
# (`ParticipantCount < 500`) with a field-level `max 500` to satisfy the
# arithmetic interval. Use a rule invariant instead.
rule ParticipantCount <= 500 because "A single meeting record cannot host more than 500 participants"

# ── States ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
state Draft initial
state Scheduled
state InProgress
state Completed terminal
state Cancelled terminal

# ── State ensures ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
in Scheduled ensure ScheduledAt is set because "A scheduled meeting must carry the timestamp it was scheduled"
in Scheduled when IsAfterHoursForHost ensure AfterHoursAcknowledged because "The host must acknowledge an after-hours meeting before it can be scheduled — host-local start {HostLocalStartTime} is outside business hours {HostBusinessHoursStart}–{HostBusinessHoursEnd}"
in InProgress ensure StartedAt is set because "An in-progress meeting must record its actual start time"
in Completed ensure EndedAt is set because "A completed meeting must record its actual end time"
in Cancelled ensure CancelledAt is set because "A cancelled meeting must record the cancellation timestamp"
in Cancelled ensure CancellationReason is set because "A cancelled meeting must record why it was cancelled"

# ── Construction event ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
event Create(
    MeetingId as string notempty maxlength 50,
    Title as string notempty maxlength 200,
    HostName as string notempty maxlength 200,
    HostEmail as ~string notempty maxlength 200,
    HostTimezone as timezone,
    StartUtc as instant,
    Duration as duration,
    BizStart as time,
    BizEnd as time) initial

on Create ensure Create.Duration.totalSeconds > 0 because "Meeting duration must be positive"
on Create ensure Create.BizEnd > Create.BizStart because "Host business hours end must be after start"

# ── Other events ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
event AddParticipant(Email as ~string notempty maxlength 200, Tz as timezone)
event RemoveParticipant(Email as ~string notempty maxlength 200)
event AcknowledgeAfterHours
event Reschedule(NewStartUtc as instant, NewDuration as duration)
event Schedule
event StartMeeting
event EndMeeting
event Cancel(Reason as string notempty)

on Reschedule ensure Reschedule.NewDuration.totalSeconds > 0 because "Rescheduled duration must be positive"

# ── Construction row ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
on Create
    -> set MeetingId = Create.MeetingId
    -> set Title = Create.Title
    -> set HostName = Create.HostName
    -> set HostEmail = Create.HostEmail
    -> set HostTimezone = Create.HostTimezone
    -> set MeetingStartUtc = Create.StartUtc
    -> set MeetingDuration = Create.Duration
    -> set HostBusinessHoursStart = Create.BizStart
    -> set HostBusinessHoursEnd = Create.BizEnd
    -> append MeetingLog "Meeting {Create.MeetingId} drafted — host {Create.HostName} ({Create.HostTimezone})"

# ── Entry hooks ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Every phase records its timestamp on state entry — no need to repeat the
# `set XxxAt = now()` line on every inbound transition row. The entry hook
# fires on every inbound edge, including back-edges if any were declared.
to Scheduled -> set ScheduledAt = now()
to InProgress -> set StartedAt = now()
to Completed -> set EndedAt = now()
to Cancelled -> set CancelledAt = now()

# ── Participant management ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Duplicate guard. `ParticipantEmails contains AddParticipant.Email` is
# evaluated case-insensitively because `ParticipantEmails` is `set of
# ~string` — a caller who first added "Alice@example.com" and then tries
# again as "alice@example.com" is rejected here, before the counter
# increments and the lookup tombstone bloats.
from Draft, Scheduled on AddParticipant when ParticipantEmails contains AddParticipant.Email
    -> reject "Participant {AddParticipant.Email} is already on this meeting"
from Draft, Scheduled on AddParticipant when ParticipantCount >= 500
    -> reject "Maximum 500 participants per meeting — current count is {ParticipantCount}"
from Draft, Scheduled on AddParticipant
    -> add ParticipantZones AddParticipant.Tz
    -> add ParticipantEmails AddParticipant.Email
    -> put ParticipantZoneByEmail AddParticipant.Email = AddParticipant.Tz
    -> set ParticipantCount = ParticipantCount + 1
    -> append MeetingLog "Added {AddParticipant.Email} ({AddParticipant.Tz})"
    -> no transition

# Note: lookup deletion is unsupported (BUG-002). The ParticipantEmails set
# is the canonical membership record; the lookup entry stays as a tombstone
# until the meeting record is itself archived. Reads should always filter
# through ParticipantEmails. The `contains` guard below uses CI semantics
# from `set of ~string`, so a caller who invited "Alice@…" can remove the
# entry by typing "ALICE@…" without the system claiming they were never on
# the meeting.
from Draft, Scheduled on RemoveParticipant when not (ParticipantEmails contains RemoveParticipant.Email)
    -> reject "Participant {RemoveParticipant.Email} is not on this meeting"
from Draft, Scheduled on RemoveParticipant
    -> remove ParticipantEmails RemoveParticipant.Email
    -> set ParticipantCount = ParticipantCount - 1
    -> append MeetingLog "Removed {RemoveParticipant.Email}"
    -> no transition

# ── After-hours acknowledgement ───────────────────────────────────────────────
from Draft on AcknowledgeAfterHours
    -> set AfterHoursAcknowledged = true
    -> append MeetingLog "After-hours scheduling acknowledged by host"
    -> no transition

# ── Reschedule (while still in Draft or Scheduled) ────────────────────────────
# Rescheduling resets the after-hours acknowledgement — if the new time is
# still after-hours, the host must acknowledge again before the meeting can
# advance to Scheduled. (The state ensure on Scheduled catches the lapse.)
from Draft, Scheduled on Reschedule
    -> set MeetingStartUtc = Reschedule.NewStartUtc
    -> set MeetingDuration = Reschedule.NewDuration
    -> set AfterHoursAcknowledged = false
    -> append MeetingLog "Rescheduled — host-local start now {HostLocalStartTime} on {HostLocalDate}"
    -> no transition

# ── Schedule ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The Scheduled state ensure enforces the after-hours acknowledgement
# requirement, so no row-level guard is needed — if IsAfterHoursForHost is
# true and AfterHoursAcknowledged is false, the state ensure rejects.
from Draft on Schedule
    -> append MeetingLog "Scheduled for {HostLocalStart} ({HostTimezone})"
    -> transition Scheduled

# ── Meeting lifecycle ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
from Scheduled on StartMeeting
    -> append MeetingLog "Meeting started"
    -> transition InProgress

from InProgress on EndMeeting
    -> append MeetingLog "Meeting ended"
    -> transition Completed

# ── Cancellation ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Cancellation is allowed from any non-terminal state — until the meeting
# has run to completion, it can be called off.
from Draft, Scheduled, InProgress on Cancel
    -> set CancellationReason = Cancel.Reason
    -> append MeetingLog "Cancelled: {Cancel.Reason}"
    -> transition Cancelled
